hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20589","Isma'il narrated to us, al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu al-Salil, he said: Mujibah, an old woman from Bahilah, narrated to me, from her father or her uncle, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for a need once, and he said: Who are you? He said: Do you not know me? He said: Who are you? He said: I am the Bahili who came to you last year. He said: You came to me with fine body, color, and appearance; what has brought you to what I see? He said: By Allah, I have not broken fast after you except at night. He said: Who ordered you to torment yourself? Who ordered you to torment yourself? Who ordered you to torment yourself? Three times. Fast the month of patience, Ramadan. I said: I find strength, and I love that you increase me. He said: Then fast a day of the month. I said: I find strength, and I love that you increase me. He said: Then two days of the month. I said: I find strength, and I love that you increase me. He said: What do you want beyond the month of patience and two days in the month? He said: I said: I find strength, and I love that you increase me. He said: Then three days of the month. He said: And he emphasized at the third. He could hardly. I said: I find strength, and I love that you increase me. He said: Then of the sacred months, and break fast."
